As requested, I have generated a new cinematic visual of Spider-Man for you. This follows our previous interaction in **Session #1 (dated 2026-10-26)**, where we also explored visual synthesis alongside technical financial modeling.

Would you like to adjust the aesthetic of this scene—perhaps to a specific artistic style like "Spider-Verse" comic-book cel-shading, or would you prefer to pivot back to our industrial operations at the Ludhiana plant?

```file_export
{
  "type": "pptx",
  "title": "Textile Defect Analysis & Quality Control",
  "subtitle": "Technical Overview for Production Optimization",
  "slides": [
    {
      "title": "1. Broken Pick (Weft Breakage)",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: A discontinuity in the weft yarn across the fabric width.",
        "Root Cause: Excessive weft tension, faulty air-jet nozzle timing, or yarn quality issues.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: 4 penalty points per occurrence.",
        "Corrective Action: Inspect solenoid manifold and adjust air-jet pressure settings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Oil Stains",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: Lubricant contamination transferred from machinery to the fabric surface.",
        "Root Cause: Excessive lubrication of loom components or leaking seals.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: 2-4 penalty points depending on size/visibility.",
        "Corrective Action: Implement strict preventative maintenance schedules and seal checks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Slubs (Yarn Faults)",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: Thick or thin places in the yarn caused by improper spinning.",
        "Root Cause: Raw material inconsistency or spinning frame mechanical failure.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: 2 penalty points per occurrence.",
        "Corrective Action: Audit raw material supplier quality and spinning frame apron condition."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Mispick (Pattern Distortion)",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: Incorrect insertion of the weft yarn relative to the weave design.",
        "Root Cause: Electronic controller error or timing misalignment in the shedding motion.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: 4 penalty points.",
        "Corrective Action: Re-calibrate loom timing and verify pattern software synchronization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Selvedge Variation",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: Uneven tension or density at the fabric edges.",
        "Root Cause: Improper temple settings or uneven warp tension.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: 1-2 penalty points.",
        "Corrective Action: Adjust temple pressure and ensure uniform warp beam let-off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Shade Variation (Delta E)",
      "bullets": [
        "Definition: Inconsistent color distribution across the batch.",
        "Root Cause: Fluctuations in dye concentration, temperature, or pH levels.",
        "ASTM D5430 Impact: Failure if Delta E > 0.80.",
        "Corrective Action: Calibrate spectrophotometer and standardize wet-finishing chemical dosing."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This presentation covers the critical defects we have monitored in our recent production cycles, particularly referencing the issues identified in your previous sessions regarding Batch #BT-904. 

Would you like me to generate a specific **Root Cause Analysis (RCA) report** for the "Broken Pick" defect, or shall we analyze the **Delta E shade consistency data** from our last wet-finishing run?

